export let frontmatter = {
  "title": "How Fumadocs works",
  "description": "The framework for building documentation",
  "author": "Fuma Nama",
  "date": new Date(1715731200000)
};
export let lastModified = new Date(1759051717000);
export let structuredData = {
  "contents": [{
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "1 year ago, I was having fun with Next.js App Router.\nWhile experimenting with it on my toy No Deploy, I planned to build documentation.\nHowever, Nextra does not support App Router."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "To handle this, I implemented a small documentation site with solely Contentlayer and the new features from App Router.\nIt was working great, looked blazing-fast and minimal.\nI cloned the logic from No Deploy and built this documentation framework.\nWith a few months of development, it soon became powerful and stable."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "It was originally named next-docs, I renamed it to Fumadocs as it conflicts with Next.js Docs."
  }, {
    "heading": undefined,
    "content": "Thanks to the support from Next.js community, I've received a lot of suggestions along the way.\nFumadocs is now a framework used by my libraries and some other amazing projects."
  }, {
    "heading": "my-opinion",
    "content": "In Web development, most \"robust\" frameworks/libraries are incredibly heavy and fabulous, but it has indeed made our developer experience fancy."
  }, {
    "heading": "my-opinion",
    "content": "On top of Javascript, people built bundlers, transpilers, and even Typescript.\nIt feels very surprising that Javascript, a high-level scripting language, is more similar to assembly code in modern Web development.\nWe rarely use them without things like Webpack. This also applies to CSS, at least in my experience, I seldom use CSS without PostCSS."
  }, {
    "heading": "my-opinion",
    "content": "While they might be necessary for compatibility and DX, the landing of React Server Component and Next.js App Router made the experience even more mindblowing.\nIt feels like magic. These cunning magical frameworks, and web development miracles.\nThis kind of design is insane, but it also makes us mindlessly forget the boundaries."
  }, {
    "heading": "my-opinion",
    "content": "Beginners use Metadata API, while they have no idea how meta tag works.\nThey put server-side logic in a server component, while they have no idea how expensive the calculation is.\nEven when we looked at the code, we can't predict the result without running it in production mode.\nI saw too many of these misconceptions."
  }, {
    "heading": "my-opinion",
    "content": "This happens on many frameworks, they are overly magical.\nI wanted to make it less-magic, and straightforward at least for most Next.js developers."
  }, {
    "heading": "fumadocs-mdx",
    "content": "As the recommended content source, It is actually a webpack hack.\nSince Next.js could only optimize static imports, it first transforms your .map.ts to a file that roughly yields:"
  }, {
    "heading": "fumadocs-mdx",
    "content": "And then transforms MDX files with a custom loader. It makes all magic possible, but it doesn't have the ability of lazy-loading MDX files.\nComparing to Nextra, it might be a suboptimal approach."
  }, {
    "heading": "fumadocs-mdx",
    "content": "Nextra does it even easier, it directly transforms MDX files into pages. Because the Pages Router adapts Javascript files as a single page, it is possible.\nIn App Router, this is not possible anymore. Therefore, I didn't take this approach."
  }, {
    "heading": "fumadocs-core",
    "content": "The core of Fumadocs is a bunch of utilities and MDX plugins."
  }, {
    "heading": "fumadocs-core",
    "content": "Source API construct page trees from content source, integrated with other content providers."
  }, {
    "heading": "fumadocs-core",
    "content": "Headless components accelerate Fumadocs UI and other custom UI implementations."
  }, {
    "heading": "fumadocs-core",
    "content": "MDX plugins bring a perfect developer experience to all integrations."
  }, {
    "heading": "fumadocs-core",
    "content": "Search utilities make it way easier to implement document search."
  }, {
    "heading": "fumadocs-core",
    "content": "In addition, it has also established the definitions of Page Tree and Page Conventions.\nOverall, it is not yet a framework without Fumadocs UI."
  }, {
    "heading": "fumadocs-core",
    "content": "In my opinion, the most valuable part of the codebase is MDX plugins.\nI learned a lot more about ASTs and the eco-system of remark/rehype while working on them.\nAbsolutely an amazing experience."
  }, {
    "heading": "fumadocs-ui",
    "content": "The UI implementation of Fumadocs using Tailwind CSS and Radix UI.\nIts design system was inspired by Shadcn UI, using CSS variables for color utilities."
  }, {
    "heading": "fumadocs-ui",
    "content": "Although the structure of Fumadocs UI is even simpler than core, I've used some subtle hacks to solve the problem of \"use client\" directive.\nThe bundler I am using, TSX, can't handle nested structures like client components imported from a server component.\nTherefore, I made a little hack to build server components and client components as an individual entry, then inject import statements after the process."
  }, {
    "heading": "fumadocs-ui",
    "content": "Also it took me some time to come up with the preset approach for integrating Fumadocs UI with Tailwind CSS projects."
  }, {
    "heading": "docs-generators",
    "content": "We have a few built-in integrations, like fumadocs-openapi which takes an OpenAPI schema and output MDX files."
  }, {
    "heading": "docs-generators",
    "content": "For the OpenAPI one, it simply parses the schema and convert it to MDX file through string templates."
  }, {
    "heading": "docs-generators",
    "content": "The Typescript integration does a bit more, it obtains type information with Typescript Compiler API. Based on the information, it yields MDX files.\nYou can use it inside a server component, which is how <AutoTypeTable /> works."
  }, {
    "heading": "cicd",
    "content": "As a project with very few contributors, I built the CI/CD process as convenient as possible for a better efficiency.\nThe entire release process is handled by Changesets, and I wrote the scripts to update the template repository automatically.\nIt worked great so far."
  }, {
    "heading": "thanks",
    "content": "The Github repository of Fumadocs has reached 300 stars in 2024 March, it is a new achievement for me.\nWelcome to give it a star to support my work!"
  }, {
    "heading": "thanks",
    "content": "Original\nhttps://fuma-nama.vercel.app/blog/fumadocs"
  }],
  "headings": [{
    "id": "my-opinion",
    "content": "My Opinion"
  }, {
    "id": "fumadocs-mdx",
    "content": "Fumadocs MDX"
  }, {
    "id": "fumadocs-core",
    "content": "Fumadocs Core"
  }, {
    "id": "fumadocs-ui",
    "content": "Fumadocs UI"
  }, {
    "id": "docs-generators",
    "content": "Docs Generators"
  }, {
    "id": "cicd",
    "content": "CI/CD"
  }, {
    "id": "thanks",
    "content": "Thanks"
  }]
};
